title: Workers' Meeting
subtitle: Speak to the factories and the garrison.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: rally_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rally_timer = 3
go-to: bol_crowd if bolshevik >= 55 and bol_regime = 0 and phase <= 2; cheka_crowd if repression >= 30 and bol_regime = 1; main_rally if (bolshevik < 55 or bol_regime = 1 or phase > 2) and (repression < 30 or bol_regime = 0)

@bol_crowd

Bolshevik agitators have packed the hall. The soldiers in the front rows have been told that we are the party of the offensive and the bourgeoisie. They are shouting down the platform.

- @appeal: Stay on the platform and argue it out.
- @militia_guard: Have the workers' militia clear the hall.
- @cancel: Cancel the meeting.
- @easy_discard

@appeal
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2, soldiers: -1});
RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, 0);
!}

We stayed, and we were heard out by about half of the hall. A speech to a hostile crowd does not win it over, but a few workers who came to jeer left asking questions.

@militia_guard
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -2, soldiers: -2});
RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: 2, soviet_democracy: -1});
!}

The militia cleared the hall. By the evening, the Bolshevik papers were writing that the Mensheviks had set armed guards on workers.

@cancel
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -2});
RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: 1});
!}

The hall was left to the crowd. It is a defeat, and everyone knows it.

@cheka_crowd

A detachment of the Cheka has arrived at the factory gates and is asking for the names of the speakers.

- @speak_anyway: Speak anyway.
- @cancel_cheka: Cancel the meeting.
- @easy_discard

@speak_anyway
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3});
RO.add(Q, {repression: 2, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 0, 2);
!}

The meeting went ahead. The workers heard us out, and the Cheka took down the names of those who stayed to ask questions. Some will pay for it.

@cancel_cheka
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -1});
!}

We will find a hall that does not have the Cheka at the gate.

@main_rally

A meeting at a factory or a barracks is the party's oldest form of political education. What is the theme?

- @defence: Defend the revolution, and the army that defends it.
- @peace: Peace without annexations, and bread.
- @democracy: Unity of the whole democracy, and the Soviets as its organs.
- @unions: The eight-hour day, the unions and the factory committees.
- @local: Whatever the audience is asking about.
- @easy_discard

@defence
view-if: at_war = 1
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2, soldiers: 2, middle: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 3, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -1, 4);
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 2, war_weariness: 1});
!}

The defencist line fits the mood of the officers and the educated public. It does not fit the mood of the trenches.

@peace
view-if: at_war = 1
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4, soldiers: 4});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -1, 3);
RO.add(Q, {army_discipline: -1});
!}

The soldiers cheered. The phrase "peace without annexations" is the Soviet's own and nobody can call it Bolshevik.

@democracy
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2, railway: 3, soldiers: 1});
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 2, rel_sr: 3, rel_lsr: 1});
!}

We spoke for the Soviets as the free organs of the whole people, from the Mensheviks to the Left SRs. The railwaymen applauded the loudest.

@unions
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 5, railway: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -3);
RO.add(Q, {ruble: -1, rel_kad: -1});
!}

The factory committees and the unions are the workers' own organisations. They like to be told so, and employers like to hear it less.

@local
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, soldiers: 1, railway: 1});
!}

We answered the questions that were asked: prices, the bread queue, the soldiers' families. It was not a great speech, but it was heard.
